-          <p>CI works with structured records about observations and changes. It does not connect directly to a language model, retrieve logs, inspect a host, query a database, or provide an Ollama or cloud API adapter. BACON is a prospective integration target; no adapter or compatibility result is included. A future integration would need a separately specified evidence-collection and admission path.</p>
+          <p>CI works with structured records about observations and changes. It does not connect directly to a language model, retrieve logs, inspect a host, query a database, or provide an Ollama or cloud API adapter. Beacon (Beacon Profile v0.1, DOI 10.5281/zenodo.18933553) is a prospective integration target; no adapter or compatibility result is included. (Corrected 19 November 2026: the deposited v1.0.0 files misspell this name as "BACON".) A future integration would need a separately specified evidence-collection and admission path.</p>
           <p>An interval contributes to verified duration only when it is admitted and explicitly marked eligible for duration. Merely admitting a record does not make the entire interval covered. Evidence at two endpoints also does not automatically establish everything between them. Known pauses need positive supporting evidence; unexplained time stays a gap. Eligible participation overlapping a known pause is rejected.</p>
           <p>For the exact contract, read the <a href="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Kot141078/advanced-global-intelligence/main/publications/continuity-instrument-v1-0-0/package/PDFs/03_CI_Technical_Specification_EN.pdf">technical specification</a> and <a href="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Kot141078/advanced-global-intelligence/main/publications/continuity-instrument-v1-0-0/package/PDFs/04_CI_Implementation_and_Reproducibility_EN.pdf">implementation and reproducibility guide</a>.</p>
